<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">classes</ansi>

A class is what your archetype becomes. Your archetype (cleric, warrior, witch...)
is your lineage and never changes. At level 10 you promote to an advanced
class on one of three routes, and at level 30 some routes promote again to an
elite class. Each class adds ranks, new abilities that arrive at fixed
levels, and every <ansi fg="command">talent</ansi> you choose adds a little more. Companions promote
and choose talents the same way.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Commands</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">class</ansi>                      your class, its ranks so far and what comes next
  <ansi fg="command">class [member]</ansi>             the same for a companion
  <ansi fg="command">class paths [member]</ansi>       the routes open to a lineage, and what each asks
  <ansi fg="command">class promote [member] [class]</ansi>
                             preview a promotion; add <ansi fg="command">confirm</ansi> to make it
  <ansi fg="command">talent</ansi>                     your talents (see <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>)

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">The three routes</ansi>

Most lineages have a good route (alignment +30 or higher), an evil route
(-30 or lower) and a neutral route that asks nothing. The Samurai, Halberdier, Shaman, Doll Master and Gryphon Rider,
neutral lineages, each have three routes and no gate at all. The gate is checked
when you promote. Once you have promoted, you keep your class even if your
alignment moves; only the next promotion asks again. Routes are final: there
is no switching to another.

  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Lineage</ansi>   <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Good</ansi>         <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Neutral</ansi>      <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Evil</ansi>
  Cleric    Priest       Druid        Blood Priest
  Warrior   Knight       Mercenary    Blackguard
  Samurai   -            Kensai, Hatamoto and Ronin, all open to any alignment
  Halberdier -           Sweeper, Vanguard and Valkyrie, all open to any alignment
  Gryphon Rider -        Gryphon Knight, Skyscout and Wyvern Rider, all open to any alignment
  Shaman    -            Stormcaller, Mistweaver and Earthspeaker, all open to any alignment
  Doll Master -          Puppeteer, Golemancer and Marionettist, all open to any alignment
  Witch     Hedge Witch  Coven Sage   Hag
  Wizard    Theurgist    Arcanist     Warlock
  Ranger    Warden       Hunter       Stalker
  Rogue     Scout        Duelist      Assassin

Elite classes (level 30 and on): Hierarch, Elder Druid and Demonologist
(clerics), Paladin, Warlord and Dread Knight (warriors), Pathfinder,
Swordmaster and Nightblade (rogues), Sentinel, Marksman and Ravager (rangers);
see <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>. The elite classes of the other routes are still to come: their
lineages keep their advanced class's ranks until then.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

A rank is a gift that arrives at a set level: a new spell, a bigger number, a
new way to fight. Ranks are gained automatically and stack up along a route,
so an elite class keeps its advanced class's ranks. The level-up report names
each rank you just reached and what it does, then the next rank, talent or
promotion. Spells a rank teaches are learned as soon
as you reach it.

Routes in depth: <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help rogue-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help ranger-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help cleric-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help warrior-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help samurai-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help halberdier-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help dollmaster-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help shaman-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help gryphon-rider-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help summoning</ansi>.

